  "label": "Watermelon and Fried Chicken Stereotype",
  "description": "A derogatory racial stereotype historically used to demean Black people, portraying them as lazy, uneducated, and overly fond of fried chicken and watermelon — often implying they are 'simple' or 'childlike' in their tastes and behavior. This stereotype is rooted in racist caricatures and has been used to justify discrimination and systemic oppression.",
